            "text": "Cutoff date: 2017-12-31\n\nQuestion: which of the candidate genes below will be established, in work published on or after the cutoff date, as regulators of fetal hemoglobin (HbF) in human erythroid cells? \"Established\" means published functional evidence that perturbing the gene changes HbF.\n\nFor each candidate gene, do exactly one of two things.\n\n1. Claim it. Give a confidence between 0 and 1 that the gene's role is established after the cutoff, the IDs of the evidence rows that support the claim, and a one-sentence rationale.\n2. Refuse it. If what was known before the cutoff does not support a claim, list the gene under refusals with a one-sentence reason. Refusing is a correct answer when the evidence is not there.\n\nOrder claims from most to least confident. Cite only IDs that appear in the evidence given to you below. Never invent an ID.\n\nCandidate genes:\nASH1L\nATF4\nCHD3\nDNMT1\nDNMT3A\nDNMT3B\nEIF2AK1\nEIF2AK2\nEIF2AK3\nEIF2AK4\nEIF2S1\nEPAS1\nFOXO3\nGATAD2A\nGATAD2B\nHDAC2\nHIC2\nIGF2BP1\nKMT5A\nLIN28B\nMAP3K7\nMAPK1\nMBD2\nMBD3\nMTA1\nMTA2\nMTA3\nNFE2\nNFIX\nNR2C1\nNR2C2\nPGRMC1\nRBBP4\nRBBP7\nSMAD1\nSMAD5\nTET2\nVHL\nZBTB33\nZNF143\nZNF410\n\nEvidence:\nNo evidence rows are provided up front. Use the tools to query a graph that holds only records dated before the cutoff. You may make at most 40 tool calls in total, so spend them on the genes where a closer look could change your answer. Every tool result names its rows by ID. Cite only IDs that a tool returned to you. When you have finished, reply with the answer and nothing else.\n",
